# KSI-CMT-VTD / KSI-MLA-EVC / KSI-SVC-ACM: AWS Config Continuous Recording
# Validates that AWS Config is continuously recording all resource types
# including global IAM resources, delivering successfully, and that
# the Config IAM role is correctly scoped:
# - Config recorder: active, all supported, global types, CONTINUOUS
# - Config IAM role: trusts config.amazonaws.com with managed policy

META
    esp_id `ksi-cmt-vtd-mla-evc-config-recorder-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `aws`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-CMT-VTD / KSI-MLA-EVC / KSI-SVC-ACM: AWS Config Continuous Recording`
    description `Validates AWS Config is continuously recording all resource configurations including global IAM resources and delivering successfully`
    author `example-security`
    tags `aws,config,iam,fedramp,KSI-CMT-VTD,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-VTD,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-VTD,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `AWS:us-east-1:logging-infrastructure`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Ensure AWS Config recorder is set to all_supported = true with include_global_resource_types = true and recording = true.`

    component_id `comp-aws-logging`

    impl_KSI_CMT_VTD `Validation throughout deployment is confirmed by verifying that AWS Config continuously records the configuration state of all supported resource types, including global IAM resources. This provides a continuous configuration history that enables detection of any configuration drift from the approved baseline across the full resource inventory.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Configuration evaluation is validated by confirming the AWS Config recorder is actively recording (recording = true) with a last delivery status of SUCCESS, and that the recording frequency is CONTINUOUS rather than periodic. This ensures configuration changes are captured in near real-time rather than on a scheduled basis, supporting timely detection of unauthorized configuration changes.`

    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Automated configuration management capability is validated by confirming AWS Config is recording all resource types including global IAM resources, providing the configuration inventory foundation required for automated compliance evaluation via Config rules. The Config IAM role is confirmed to trust only config.amazonaws.com, ensuring configuration recording authorization is scoped to the Config service.`

META_END

DEF
    VAR aws_region string `us-east-1`

    OBJECT config_recorder
        recorder_name `example-org-config-recorder`
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    OBJECT config_role
        role_name `example-org-config-role`
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    # Config recorder: active, all resources, global types, continuous
    STATE recorder_compliant
        found boolean = true
        recording boolean = true
        all_supported boolean = true
        include_global_resource_types boolean = true
        recording_frequency string = `CONTINUOUS`
        last_status string = `SUCCESS`
    STATE_END

    # Config role: trusts config.amazonaws.com, has managed policy attached
    STATE config_role_compliant
        found boolean = true
        attached_policy_count int >= 1
        record
            field AssumeRolePolicyDocument.Statement.0.Principal.Service string = `config.amazonaws.com`
            field AssumeRolePolicyDocument.Statement.0.Effect string = `Allow`
            field AssumeRolePolicyDocument.Statement.0.Action string = `sts:AssumeRole`
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN aws_config_recorder
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF recorder_compliant
            OBJECT_REF config_recorder
        CTN_END

        CTN aws_iam_role
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF config_role_compliant
            OBJECT_REF config_role
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
